BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:56c5c3926a58d0c6c11638d52658f9a3799882f4@pushpin.city
DTSTAMP:20261128T153847Z
DTSTART:20270130T200000Z
DTEND:20270130T220000Z
SUMMARY:TLI Presents: Berkshire Bach Portals—Working Musician—J.S. Bach
  Plays the Berkshires
LOCATION:Tanglewood\, 297 West St\, Lenox\, MA 01240
DESCRIPTION:Studio E\, Linde Center for Music and Learning\nPresented in co
 llaboration with Berkshire Bach Society\, Working Musician—J.S. Bach Pla
 ys the Berkshires\, is a short film about the evolving significance of Bac
 h’s music in today's culture\, told through the lens of Berkshire Bach a
 nd the way its performances come together. The film is by documentarian An
 thony Rossello and features interviews with pianist Simone Dinnerstein\, B
 BS Artistic Director Eugene Drucker\, composer and music personality Bruce
  Adolphe\, and critic Tim Page on what makes Bach’s music important for 
 modern listeners. It includes telling anecdotes from Bach’s life and fol
 lows the preparations for the BBS signature series Bach at New Year’s fe
 aturing the six ‘Brandenburg’ Concertos. After the presentation\, Euge
 ne Drucker hosts a conversation with the filmmaker\, the performers\, and 
 the audience.\nhttps://www.bso.org/events/jan-30-tli-pres-berkshire-bac\nF
 rom Pushpin Western Mass: https://pushpin.city/westernma/
URL:https://www.bso.org/events/jan-30-tli-pres-berkshire-bac
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
